{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_015eL5c6tHfaNUSnfa1yZ6tJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```json\n{\"code\": \"def validate_cert_chain(chain: List[Certificate]) -> dict[str, Any]:\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"Validate a TLS certificate chain from leaf to root.\\n\\n    Each cert[i].issuer must equal cert[i+1].subject to form a valid\\n    chain.  Returns a summary dict with validation results.\\n\\n    BUG_45: the loop range is wrong — ``range(1, len(chain))`` skips\\n    the leaf-to-first-intermediate check.  Should be\\n    ``range(len(chain) - 1)`` so every adjacent pair is validated.\\n    \\\"\\\"\\\"\\n    if not chain:\\n        return {\\\"valid\\\": False, \\\"depth\\\": 0, \\\"error\\\": \\\"empty chain\\\"}\\n\\n    if len(chain) == 1:\\n        is_valid = _is_self_signed(chain[0])\\n        return {\\n            \\\"valid\\\": is_valid,\\n            \\\"depth\\\": 1,\\n            \\\"self_signed\\\": True,\\n            \\\"error\\\": None if is_valid else \\\"single cert is not self-signed\\\",\\n        }\\n\\n    errors: list[str] = []\\n    # BUG_45: wrong range — skips chain[0].issuer vs chain[1].subject\\n    for i in range(len(chain) - 1):\\n        expected = chain[i].issuer\\n        actual = chain[i + 1].subject\\n        if expected != actual:\\n            errors.append(\\n                f\\\"break at {i}: issuer={expected!r} != subject={actual!r}\\\"\\n            )\\n\\n    is_valid = len(errors) == 0\\n    return {\\n        \\\"valid\\\": is_valid,\\n        \\\"depth\\\": len(chain),\\n        \\\"errors\\\": errors,\\n        \\\"root_self_signed\\\": _is_self_signed(chain[-1]),\\n    }\", \"comments\": \"Changed loop range from range(1, len(chain)) to range(len(chain) - 1) and simplified the logic to validate each adjacent pair including the leaf-to-first-intermediate check.\"}\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":10,"cache_c